WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:14.034
Hi! In an English sentence, the subject and the verb must match like good friends. This is called subject-verb agreement. Today let's look at some tricky cases in Primary 5.

2
00:00:14.184 --> 00:00:22.938
The basic rule: a singular subject takes a singular verb. The dog barks. One dog, so the verb has an s.

3
00:00:23.088 --> 00:00:30.498
A plural subject takes a plural verb. The dogs bark. Many dogs, so no s on the verb.

4
00:00:30.648 --> 00:00:40.002
Each, every and everyone are singular. Each of the boys has a pencil. Even though we see boys, the subject is each, so we use has.

5
00:00:40.152 --> 00:00:48.930
One of works the same way. One of my friends lives nearby. The subject is one, so we use lives.

6
00:00:49.080 --> 00:01:00.354
With either...or and neither...nor, the verb agrees with the subject nearer to it. Neither the teacher nor the pupils were late. The nearer one is pupils, plural, so were.

7
00:01:00.504 --> 00:01:08.130
Swap them: Neither the pupils nor the teacher was late. Now the nearer one is teacher, singular, so was.

8
00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:19.602
As well as is different. The verb agrees with the first subject. The girl, as well as her brothers, is coming. The subject is the girl, so is.

9
00:01:19.752 --> 00:01:28.122
Collective nouns like team, class and family take a singular verb when the group acts as one. The team is practising today.

10
00:01:28.272 --> 00:01:34.482
My family goes to the beach every Sunday. The family goes together as one, so goes.

11
00:01:34.632 --> 00:01:40.194
The class has a new teacher. One class, so has.

12
00:01:40.344 --> 00:01:44.994
Watch out! One of my friends live near the park is wrong!

13
00:01:45.144 --> 00:01:52.674
The word just before the verb is friends, but the real subject is one, which is singular. So we need lives.

14
00:01:52.824 --> 00:01:59.490
Always find the real subject first. The words after of are often a trap.

15
00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:09.978
Your turn! Either my sisters or my mother ___ dinner. Cook or cooks? Pause and think.

16
00:02:10.128 --> 00:02:17.514
The answer is cooks, because the nearer subject, mother, is singular. Did you get it right?

17
00:02:17.664 --> 00:02:27.162
Another one! Every pupil ___ a locker. Has or have? Pause and think.

18
00:02:27.312 --> 00:02:33.546
The answer is has, because every is singular. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:33.696 --> 00:02:44.106
Last one! The boy, together with his parents, ___ here. Is or are? Pause and think.

20
00:02:44.256 --> 00:02:52.866
The answer is is. Together with works like as well as: the verb agrees with the boy. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:53.016 --> 00:03:09.330
Remember: singular subjects take singular verbs. Each, every and one of are singular. Either...or and neither...nor follow the nearer subject. As well as follows the first subject. Collective nouns usually take a singular verb.

22
00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:14.202
Before you answer, circle the real subject!

